WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 009, en. Timings are estimates from the script until the clip is rendered.

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:14.000
<v Amy Williams>Bore da, John. The tithe men left a copy of their schedule. Landough, Cogan and Leckwith, and your name down the occupier column, over and over.

2
00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:24.350
<v Amy Williams>Thirty-six parcels. Thirty-three are Bute land: a hundred and nineteen acres, nought roods, six perches. Three little ones are glebe, church land: two roods, twenty-four perches.

3
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:34.700
<v John Williams: the c.1841 tithe occupier>Add them and you get a hundred and nineteen acres, two roods, thirty perches. Every field I walk, written down by a man with a chain.

4
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:44.665
<v Amy Williams>And not a word about a lease, or a term, or what rent we pay. It shows who farms which field. That's all it shows.

5
00:00:45.015 --> 00:00:55.785
<v John Williams: the c.1841 tithe occupier>They'll finish the plan next year, 'forty-two, and it'll lie with the parish papers. Whether these fields are number nineteen on the 'twenty-four plan, it won't tell you.

6
00:00:56.135 --> 00:01:01.904
<v Amy Williams>Nor where the hedges will run in thirty years. Paper moves slower than hedges, John.

7
00:01:06.254 --> 00:01:13.177
<v Gwen>Twenty-third of December, and the house quiet as the churchyard. Sixty-five she was, John. Sixty-five, here in Llandough.

8
00:01:13.527 --> 00:01:20.450
<v John Williams: the c.1841 tithe occupier>She kept this kitchen through the tithe men and every winter since. I'll not have her written small.

9
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:30.800
<v Gwen>The paper will print her the way it prints widows: 'relict of the late Mr. John Williams, Great House farm.' The farm's own name, in print.

10
00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:35.765
<v John Williams: the c.1841 tithe occupier>Great House. Tŷ Mawr. Whatever the estate calls it in its books.

11
00:01:36.115 --> 00:01:45.731
<v Gwen>Cardiff Times, sixteenth of July, nineteen-oh-four. John Williams, 'of Llandough Farm'. And here: 'He succeeded his father in the occupancy of the farm in 1855.'

12
00:01:46.081 --> 00:01:59.158
<v Gwen>Mind what it gives you and what it doesn't. Llandough Farm, it prints, not Great House. That he's the Great House John is our own reckoning, matched against the census, not the paper's words.

13
00:01:59.508 --> 00:02:10.662
<v Gwen>Father to son in one line of print. No word of when the father went, nor what he left. Only that in 'fifty-five the son took the farm on.
